          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Which scale helped you measure the length of the screws accurately? Why?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.429,
            0.774,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the meaning of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 \\frac { 7 } { 1 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " cm (the length of the first screw)?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.476,
            0.848,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As seen on the ruler, the unit length between two consecutive numbers is divided into 10 equal parts. To get the length "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2   \\frac { 7 } { 1 0 }   \\mathrm { c m }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , we go from 0 to 2 and then take seven parts of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{1}{10}."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The length of the screw is 2 cm and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 7 } { 1 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " cm. Similarly, we can make sense of the length "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3   \\frac { 2 } { 1 0 }   \\mathrm { c m }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We read "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 \\frac { 7 } { 1 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " cm as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "two and seven-tenth centimeters",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 \\frac { 2 } { 1 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " cm as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "three and two-tenth centimeters",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.667,
            0.847,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Can you explain why the unit was divided into smaller parts to measure the screws?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.727,
            0.848,
            0.789
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Measure the following objects using a scale and write their measurements in centimeters (as shown earlier for the lengths of the screws): pen, sharpener, and any other object of your choice."
            }
          ]
        },
